{"slug":"zero-one-knapsack-value","title":"Pack the Bag With the Most Valuable Items","topic":"dp","difficulty":"medium","order":736,"tags":["dp","knapsack","0-1-knapsack"],"timeLimitMs":2000,"concept":{"title":"The classic knapsack: for each item decide take or leave, with a table over the room left","body":["A thief has a bag that carries a total weight of at most `cap`. There are `n` items, each with a weight and a value, and each item exists **once**. Which items should be taken to get the largest total value? With the items (weight, value) `(1, 15) (3, 20) (4, 30)` and the capacity `4` the best is the first and the second item: value 35, weight 4. (Taking the most valuable item first is not always right: the item `(4, 30)` alone gives only 30.)","Let `best(c)` be the largest value that fits into the weight `c`, starting with `best(c) = 0` for all `c` (no items yet). Process the items one at a time. For an item with the weight `w` and the value `v`: for each capacity `c >= w` we may take the item (value `best(c - w) + v`, where `best(c - w)` describes the bag **without** this item) or leave it (value `best(c)`). So **`best(c) = max(best(c), best(c - w) + v)`**. The loop over `c` must go **downwards**, so that `best(c - w)` has not yet been changed by the same item.",{"code":"best = [0] * (cap + 1)\nfor w, v in items:\n    for c in range(cap, w - 1, -1):          # downwards: each item at most once\n        best[c] = max(best[c], best[c - w] + v)\nprint(best[cap])"},"This is the template of all \"choose items under a limit\" problems. The time is O(n * cap) = 2 million steps at most, the memory O(cap). (A greedy choice by value per weight is wrong for such items, because items cannot be split.) Because `best` is a maximum over \"weight at most `c`\", the answer is simply `best[cap]`."]},"statement":["There are `n` items; the item `i` has the weight `w[i]` and the value `v[i]`. A bag can carry a total weight of at most `cap`. Each item can be taken at most once. Print the largest total value of the items that fit in the bag."],"inputFormat":["The first line has `n` and `cap`: the number of items and the capacity of the bag.","Each of the next `n` lines has two numbers: the weight and the value of one item."],"outputFormat":["Print the largest total value."],"constraints":["1 <= n <= 200","1 <= cap <= 10000","1 <= weight <= 1000","1 <= value <= 1000000"],"examples":[{"input":"3 4\n1 15\n3 20\n4 30\n","output":"35\n","note":"Take the first two items: weight 4, value 35."},{"input":"2 5\n6 100\n5 7\n","output":"7\n","note":"Only the second item fits: 7."}],"hints":["Let best(c) be the largest value that fits into the weight c, starting from all zeros.","For every item update best(c) = max(best(c), best(c - w) + v) for c from the capacity down to w.","Going downwards makes sure that each item is used only once."],"starter":{"python":"import sys\ninput = sys.stdin.readline\n\nn, cap = map(int, input().split())\nitem = [list(map(int, input().split())) for _ in range(n)]\n\n# Your code here\n","cpp":"#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <string>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint main() {\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n\n    long long n;\n    long long cap;\n    cin >> n >> cap;\n    vector<vector<long long>> item(n, vector<long long>(2));\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n        for (int j = 0; j < 2; j++) {\n            cin >> item[i][j];\n        }\n    }\n\n    // Your code here\n\n    return 0;\n}\n","java":"import java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    static BufferedReader in = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n    static StringTokenizer tokens = new StringTokenizer(\"\");\n\n    static String next() throws IOException {\n        while (!tokens.hasMoreTokens()) {\n            tokens = new StringTokenizer(in.readLine());\n        }\n        return tokens.nextToken();\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        long n = Long.parseLong(next());\n        long cap = Long.parseLong(next());\n        long[][] item = new long[(int) n][2];\n        for (int i = 0; i < item.length; i++) {\n            for (int j = 0; j < item[i].length; j++) {\n                item[i][j] = Long.parseLong(next());\n            }\n        }\n\n        // Your code here\n    }\n}\n"},"solution":{"explanation":["best(c) is the largest value that fits into the weight c; every item updates the table from the top downwards with best(c) = max(best(c), best(c - w) + v), so that each item is used at most once. The answer is best(cap)."],"complexity":"Time O(n * cap), space O(cap).","code":{"python":"import sys\ninput = sys.stdin.readline\n\nn, cap = map(int, input().split())\nitem = [list(map(int, input().split())) for _ in range(n)]\n\nbest = [0] * (cap + 1)\nfor w, v in item:\n    for c in range(cap, w - 1, -1):\n        if best[c - w] + v > best[c]:\n            best[c] = best[c - w] + v\nprint(best[cap])\n","cpp":"#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <string>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint main() {\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n\n    long long n;\n    long long cap;\n    cin >> n >> cap;\n    vector<vector<long long>> item(n, vector<long long>(2));\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n        for (int j = 0; j < 2; j++) {\n            cin >> item[i][j];\n        }\n    }\n\n    vector<long long> best(cap + 1, 0);\n    for (const vector<long long>& it : item) {\n        long long w = it[0], v = it[1];\n        for (long long c = cap; c >= w; c--) {\n            best[c] = max(best[c], best[c - w] + v);\n        }\n    }\n    cout << best[cap] << \"\\n\";\n\n    return 0;\n}\n","java":"import java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    static BufferedReader in = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n    static StringTokenizer tokens = new StringTokenizer(\"\");\n\n    static String next() throws IOException {\n        while (!tokens.hasMoreTokens()) {\n            tokens = new StringTokenizer(in.readLine());\n        }\n        return tokens.nextToken();\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        long n = Long.parseLong(next());\n        long cap = Long.parseLong(next());\n        long[][] item = new long[(int) n][2];\n        for (int i = 0; i < item.length; i++) {\n            for (int j = 0; j < item[i].length; j++) {\n                item[i][j] = Long.parseLong(next());\n            }\n        }\n\n        int room = (int) cap;\n        long[] best = new long[room + 1];\n        for (int t = 0; t < n; t++) {\n            int w = (int) item[t][0];\n            long v = item[t][1];\n            for (int c = room; c >= w; c--) {\n                best[c] = Math.max(best[c], best[c - w] + v);\n            }\n        }\n        System.out.println(best[room]);\n    }\n}\n"}},"tests":[{"input":"3 4\n1 15\n3 20\n4 30\n","output":"35\n"},{"input":"2 5\n6 100\n5 7\n","output":"7\n"},{"input":"1 1\n1 1\n","output":"1\n"},{"input":"1 1\n2 5\n","output":"0\n"},{"input":"10 50\n18 25\n16 5\n4 97\n20 25\n3 3\n7 74\n9 99\n3 57\n6 11\n12 39\n","output":"380\n"},{"input":"50 500\n66 751\n100 112\n59 556\n19 620\n6 503\n56 491\n26 573\n76 580\n29 600\n6 844\n21 469\n92 6\n86 332\n20 793\n59 913\n75 201\n65 735\n67 668\n73 902\n81 466\n26 15\n9 958\n14 819\n19 682\n71 438\n57 850\n4 802\n75 780\n61 471\n93 682\n67 467\n80 632\n72 886\n10 557\n6 928\n85 220\n79 954\n44 337\n82 754\n2 173\n21 403\n29 313\n26 943\n57 560\n95 271\n56 381\n77 238\n88 75\n22 172\n58 202\n","output":"14218\n"},{"input":"100 3000\n270 19371\n242 97792\n29 90445\n260 43114\n132 50745\n263 5439\n109 64033\n259 8907\n249 45459\n43 89670\n81 19158\n62 65493\n229 69057\n127 3269\n276 94751\n108 93667\n263 84704\n213 53044\n263 22710\n126 88868\n164 80403\n108 17486\n300 81258\n125 49491\n183 59120\n85 78582\n238 86916\n133 54996\n32 37588\n139 49385\n68 71860\n72 35832\n51 26410\n197 39255\n253 49160\n37 